# =========================================================================
# PRODUCTION DEPLOYMENT CHECKLIST  (Vercel → Settings → Environment Variables)
# =========================================================================
# These MUST be set in the Vercel *Production* environment. Missing any of the
# "required" ones is a hard crash / broken flow, not a graceful degradation.
#
#   Required for the app to run at all (auth, onboarding):
#     NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL
#     NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
#     SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY     ← Secret. Onboarding builds this client to
#                                     sign avatar URLs; absent = /onboarding 500.
#   Required before a user records / generates a message:
#     ELEVENLABS_API_KEY            ← Secret (voice clone + TTS)
#     ANTHROPIC_API_KEY             ← Secret (message text generation; paid API)
#   Auth / beta:
#     VOICE_CONSENT_REQUIRED=true   (enforce the voice-consent gate)  — config
#   Beta payments — testers walk REAL Stripe Checkout and are charged $0:
#     NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL           ← MUST be the deployment's own https URL.
#                                     It builds Stripe's success_url/cancel_url.
#                                     Unset, it falls back to
#                                     http://localhost:3100 and every tester who
#                                     finishes checkout is redirected to their
#                                     own machine — the payment succeeds and the
#                                     app never sees them come back.
#     VAULT_STRIPE_ENABLED=true
#     STRIPE_BETA_COUPON_ID=<100%-off coupon id>   ← the thing that makes it $0.
#                                     UNSET before charging real money.
#     STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET         ← Secret. Real Checkout needs a live webhook
#                                     endpoint pointed at this deployment, or the
#                                     subscription row is only written by the
#                                     success_url reconcile and every later
#                                     lifecycle event is silently dropped.
#   Keep OFF / absent for the free beta:
#     VOICE_CREATION_REQUIRES_PAYMENT
#   Must NOT be set to "false" anywhere a user can reach:
#     DEFERRED_AUDIO_ENABLED        ← defaults ON. "false" selects the control
#                                     arm, whose preview screen was never built,
#                                     so message creation 404s after a paid
#                                     generation. See src/lib/messages/cost-controls.ts.
#   NEVER set in production:
#     ENABLE_DEV_ROUTES, ENABLE_DEV_AUTH, PLAYWRIGHT_TEST_*, ENABLE_INTERNAL_DELETE
#
# Secrets (API keys, service-role key): mark "Sensitive", never prefix NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# After changing Vercel env vars, trigger a NEW deployment (redeploy or a fresh
# commit) — an existing deployment will not pick up the change.
# =========================================================================

# =========================
# Supabase
# =========================

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Server only — do not expose to browser
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# =========================
# App
# =========================

# Local: match the port you actually run `next dev` on — this is the origin
# Stripe redirects back to after checkout, so a mismatch strands the return trip.
# Production: the deployment's own https URL. Never leave it at a localhost value.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000

# =========================
# ElevenLabs (server-only)
# =========================
# No quotes. No spaces around =. Get key: elevenlabs.io → Profile → API Keys
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=

# =========================
# Anthropic (server-only)
# =========================
# Powers the Step 6 hybrid "personalized insert" (Claude Haiku) per MASTER_SPEC
# 8.7.1. Required for /api/messages/generate when the user provides a note; the
# pure-template path works without it. Get key: console.anthropic.com → API Keys
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# =========================
# Stripe (Session 7b)
# =========================
# Test-mode keys from dashboard.stripe.com → Developers → API keys while in
# Sandbox mode. Publishable key is safe in the browser; secret key is
# server-only and must never be prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=

# Webhook signing secret — required once /api/stripe/webhook lands in 7b.
# Local dev: run `stripe listen --forward-to localhost:3100/api/stripe/webhook`
# and copy the whsec_... value it prints. Production: set the production
# webhook's signing secret from the Stripe dashboard.
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# Price IDs — create Monthly ($12.99) and Annual ($119.00) recurring prices
# under the Voice Vault product in Stripe Dashboard → Products.
STRIPE_PRICE_ID_VAULT_MONTHLY=
STRIPE_PRICE_ID_VAULT_ANNUAL=

# Feature flag — 'true' routes vault checkout through real Stripe. 'false'
# returns a mock checkout URL and keeps the spine guards in mock-walk form.
# S5 go-live: flip to 'true' TOGETHER WITH VOICE_CREATION_REQUIRES_PAYMENT and
# real STRIPE_PRICE_ID_VAULT_* values (and a live STRIPE_SECRET_KEY +
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET). All three move as one lever — see docs/session-s5-golive.
#
# Beta: 'true' with test-mode keys + STRIPE_BETA_COUPON_ID below, and
# VOICE_CREATION_REQUIRES_PAYMENT left off. Testers see the real Checkout
# screen, enter a card, and are charged nothing.
VAULT_STRIPE_ENABLED=true

# Beta comp — the id of a 100%-off Stripe coupon (Dashboard → Product catalogue
# → Coupons, or `stripe coupons create --percent-off 100 --duration forever`).
# When set, every checkout is created with this discount applied and with
# payment_method_collection='always', so a card is still collected and stored.
# Leave EMPTY to charge the real price. Unset it before going live.
STRIPE_BETA_COUPON_ID=

# Feature flag (FOLLOW_UPS #22) — 'true' gates paid voice creation
# (/api/voice-profiles/[id]/start → ElevenLabs) on an active subscription
# ({trial, active}); other statuses get 402. The card-capture-before-processing
# reorder that yields `trial` before /start has landed (spine S1–S3), so this is
# safe to flip at S5 alongside VAULT_STRIPE_ENABLED. Keep OFF until then.
VOICE_CREATION_REQUIRES_PAYMENT=false

# =========================
# Playwright test account (local/dev only — do NOT use in prod)
# =========================
# Test user for automated e2e tests. Playwright signs in via
# signInWithPassword against this account to bypass magic-link auth.
# Bootstrap: create via Supabase admin API with a random password and
# user_metadata.playwright_test = true, then populate these three vars.
PLAYWRIGHT_TEST_EMAIL=
PLAYWRIGHT_TEST_PASSWORD=
PLAYWRIGHT_TEST_USER_ID=

# =========================
# Dev-only route gates — local only, NEVER set in production / Vercel
# =========================
# ENABLE_DEV_ROUTES: exposes /dev/* routes (sandboxes, visual review).
#   When unset or !== 'true', the entire /dev segment 404s (see
#   src/app/dev/layout.tsx).
# ENABLE_DEV_AUTH: additionally exposes /dev/test-auth, a credential-
#   accepting endpoint used by Playwright to sign the test account in.
#   Defense in depth: even if ENABLE_DEV_ROUTES is accidentally enabled
#   somewhere it shouldn't be, the credential endpoint requires this
#   second flag. Both must be true for /dev/test-auth to render.
ENABLE_DEV_ROUTES=
ENABLE_DEV_AUTH=

# =========================
# Step 6 — message creation
# =========================
# DEFERRED_AUDIO_ENABLED defaults to ON and should be left unset.
# Setting it to "false" selects the control arm (audio rendered inline on every
# generate). That arm's A6 preview screen was never built, so
# /messages/new/g/[generationId] returns 404 — the user pays for a full LLM +
# ElevenLabs render and lands on "We couldn't find that page". Only set it to
# "false" in a test that exercises the control arm's API behaviour.
# DEFERRED_AUDIO_ENABLED=

# =========================
# Rate Limits (optional overrides)
# =========================
# RATE_LIMIT_MAX_CLIPS_PER_PROFILE=30
# RATE_LIMIT_MAX_MESSAGES_PER_DAY=20
# RATE_LIMIT_MAX_VOICE_CREATIONS_PER_DAY=5
# RATE_LIMIT_MAX_SIGNED_URLS_PER_MINUTE=30

# =========================
# Internal Testing (do not enable in production)
# =========================
# ENABLE_INTERNAL_DELETE=true
